Why Title Insurance Matters
In today's complex real estate environment, title insurance plays a critical role in maintaining market stability. Property chains now involve more parties than ever, increasing the potential for title defects to surface unexpectedly. The average property in the U.S. has changed hands 6-8 times since records began, with each transfer presenting potential legal complications. Title insurance provides peace of mind by covering legal fees and potential losses should any undiscovered issues with the property's history emerge.

